From 103812fc33fac43dd85fd1f9dbd80049652fd912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:36:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bind CommandsService on the settings WebUI broker

Since Chromium 156, chrome://settings binds its interfaces through the
per-WebUI broker registered for settings::SettingsUI, which
BraveSettingsUI shares (GetType() is final in SettingsUI). Brave only
registered CommandsService in the old frame binder map, so the
shortcuts subpage of brave://settings/system asked for an interface the
broker did not have and the renderer was killed with a bad message.

Register CommandsService with ForWebUI<BraveSettingsUI>(), as Brave
does, and take Brave's chromium_src hook that lets a second ForWebUI()
for an already registered controller type pass the DCHECK. Add a
browsertest that opens the settings pages, system and shortcuts
included, and checks the renderer stays alive. A static_assert keeps
BraveSettingsUI member-free, since the shared broker may run its binders
on a plain SettingsUI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MwmK2juPkbC58kEi4QFeyU
